or"}]}], "member": "29733", "event": {"name": "Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37", "theme": "38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024)", "location": "Vancouver, BC, Canada", "acronym": "NeurIPS 2024", "number": "37", "start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 10]]}, "end": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 15]]}}, "container-title": ["Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 19]], "date-time": "2026-06-19T15:38:36Z", "timestamp": 1781883516000}, "score": 58.093037, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://www.proceedings.com/079017-1670.html"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.52202/079017-1670", "published": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 13]], "date-time": "2024-05-13T15:50:08Z", "timestamp": 1715615408794}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Yale University Press", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9780300207200", "type": "print"}, {"value": "9780300265248", "type": "electronic"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2022, 7, 12]]}, "abstract": "<p>This chapter shows how Elizabethan ideas about the imagination were in many ways fundamentally different from modern ones; beginning with the period's understanding of the location and function of this faculty in the brain. It first takes a look into Andreas Vesalius' groundbreaking studies in human anatomy \u2014 particularly the human brain and its capacity for imagination. Next, the chapter takes a look at how imagination was perceived as wicked, according to biblical scripture. The interpretation of dreams is then discussed, followed by a look into how Elizabethans used imagination as a means of literary creation. Focus is given on the \u2018mind's eye\u2019 or the imaginative writer's mental image-making, as well as the \u2018imagine\u2019 chorus. Finally, the chapter considers how Shakespeare in particular treated imagination.</p>", "DOI": "10.12987/yale/9780300207200.003.0008", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2023, 1, 20]], "date-time": "2023-01-20T14:40:44Z", "timestamp": 1674225644000}, "page": "218-257", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["\u2018Things Feigned in the Mind\u2019"], "prefix": "10.12987", "author": [{"given": "Helen", "family": "Hackett", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "5164", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2023, 1, 19]]}, "container-title": ["The Elizabethan Mind"], "original-title": ["\u2018Things Feigned in the Mind\u2019"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2023, 1, 20]], "date-time": "2023-01-20T14:40:45Z", "timestamp": 1674225645000}, "score": 25.684807, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://academic.oup.com/yale-scholarship-online/book/45045/chapter/385316229"}}, "subtitle": ["The Unruly Imagination"], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2022, 7, 12]]}, "ISBN": ["9780300207200", "9780300265248"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.12987/yale/9780300207200.003.0008", "published": {"date-parts": [[2022, 7, 12]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2022, 4, 2]], "date-time": "2022-04-02T01:19:43Z", "timestamp": 1648862383275}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Yale University Press", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2021, 9, 14]]}, "DOI": "10.2307/j.ctv1vbd15n.11", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2021, 8, 8]], "date-time": "2021-08-08T20:26:27Z", "timestamp": 1628454387000}, "page": "144-165", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Use Your Imagination"], "prefix": "10.2307", "member": "1121", "container-title": ["The Art of Self-Improvement"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2021, 8, 8]], "date-time": "2021-08-08T20:26:42Z", "timestamp": 1628454402000}, "score": 24.82